        "original_id": "1cefe94c-2899-5e09-9d42-84d9dc4db082",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Topics: Art Deco in the United States\n- Places: France, United States, New York City\n- Products: Empire State Building, Chrysler Building, Rockefeller Center\n\nFacts:\n- The Art Deco style originated in France just before World War I.\n- Art Deco had an important impact on architecture and design in the United States during the 1920s and 1930s.\n- The most famous Art Deco examples in the United States included New York skyscrapers such as the Empire State Building, Chrysler Building, and Rockefeller Center in New York City.\n- Rockefeller Center is a large complex of 19 high-rise commercial buildings covering 22 acres between 48th and 51st Streets in New York City.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
