        "original_id": "caf2c371-0d47-5579-99a0-6c703fe184fd",
        "text": "Page: Art Deco in the United States. Sentence: The Art Deco style, which originated in France just before World War I, had an important impact on architecture and design in the United States in the 1920s and 1930s.\nPage: Art Deco in the United States. Sentence: The most famous examples were the skyscrapers of New York, including the Empire State Building, Chrysler Building, and Rockefeller Center in New York City.\nPage: Rockefeller Center. Sentence: Rockefeller Center is a large complex consisting of 19 high-rise commercial buildings covering 22 acre between 48th and 51st Streets in New York City.",
